  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1002.11 Application Processing and Licensing Fees for the Professions Regulated by the Board of Dental Examiners. The application processing and licensing fees found in Table 1002.11, below, shall apply to the professions regulated by the board of dental examiners under RSA 317‑A:\n\nTable 1002.11 Application Processing and Licensing Fees for the Professions Regulated by the Board of Dental Examiners\n\nCategory | License Duration | Fee\n\nDentist license or dental hygienist license, application processing and licensing:\n\nActive: initial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | 2 years | $187\n\nInactive: initial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | 2 years | $93\n\nChange inactive to active | 2 years | $93\n\nLicensed dental hygienist permit to administer nitrous oxide application processing and licensing:\n\nInitial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | attached to license | $27\n\nLicensed dental hygienist permit for certified public health dental hygienist (CPHDH) or expanded function dental auxiliary (EFDA) application processing and licensing:\n\nInitial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | attached to license | $27\n\nTemporary license to provide voluntary services application processing and licensing | max. 12 months | $40\n\nTemporary license to teach or participate in research project per Den 301.05 application processing and licensing | max. 12 months | $40\n\nGeneral anesthesia, deep sedation, and moderate sedation permits application processing and licensing:\n\nInitial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | 2 years | $187\n\nFacility license application processing and licensing:\n\nInitial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | 2 years | $170\n\nSource. #13260, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 9-10-21, EXPIRED: 3-9-22\n\nNew. #13420, eff 8-8-22; ss by #13703, eff 8-1-23 (formerly Plc 1002.10); ss by #14290, eff 7-1-25, EXPIRES: 7-1-35",
